WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.631 --> 00:00:07.590
Careful of that hammer.

2
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.434
- Dory!
- Sea-Monkey has my money.

3
00:00:18.519 --> 00:00:20.770
Wake up. Get up.

4
00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:23.439
- Come on.
- Yes, I'm a natural blue.

5
00:00:23.524 --> 00:00:25.316
- Get up!
- Look out. Sharks eat fish!

6
00:00:48.215 --> 00:00:51.300
Wow. Dusty.

7
00:00:52.136 --> 00:00:54.220
The mask. Where's the mask?

8
00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:57.223
No! The mask! Get it!

9
00:00:57.307 --> 00:00:59.225
Get the mask! Get it!

10
00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:08.317
Whoo-hoo!

11
00:01:09.444 --> 00:01:11.028
Keeps going on, doesn't it?

12
00:01:11.113 --> 00:01:12.947
Echo! Echo!

13
00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:16.075
- What are you doing?
- I've lost the mask.

14
00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:18.077
- Did you drop it?
- You dropped it!

15
00:01:18.162 --> 00:01:20.705
That was my only chance of
finding my son. Now it's gone.

16
00:01:24.877 --> 00:01:27.128
Hey, Mr. Grumpy Gills.

17
00:01:28.547 --> 00:01:31.090
- When you're down, know what to do?
- I don't want to know.

18
00:01:31.175 --> 00:01:33.467
Just keep swimming.

19
00:01:33.552 --> 00:01:36.137
Just keep swimming,
swimming, swimming

20
00:01:36.221 --> 00:01:38.472
What do we do? We swim

21
00:01:38.557 --> 00:01:40.308
Dory, no singing.

22
00:01:41.018 --> 00:01:43.102
I love to swim

23
00:01:43.187 --> 00:01:46.772
And when you want to
swim you want to...

24
00:01:46.857 --> 00:01:49.817
I'm going to get stuck with
that song. It's in my head!

25
00:01:49.902 --> 00:01:51.068
Sorry.

26
00:01:53.155 --> 00:01:55.198
See anything?
Something's got me!

27
00:01:55.282 --> 00:01:57.241
- That was me. Sorry.
- Who's that?

28
00:01:57.326 --> 00:01:59.577
Who could it be? It's me.

29
00:01:59.661 --> 00:02:02.330
Are... Are
you my conscience?

30
00:02:03.415 --> 00:02:05.499
Yeah. I'm
your conscience.

31
00:02:05.584 --> 00:02:08.419
We haven't spoken for a while.
How are you?

32
00:02:08.503 --> 00:02:10.546
- Can't complain.
- Good.

33
00:02:10.631 --> 00:02:14.133
Now, Dory, I want you to tell
me, do you see anything?

34
00:02:14.218 --> 00:02:16.093
I see a...

35
00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.596
- I see a light.
- A light?

36
00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:20.806
Yeah. Over there.

37
00:02:20.891 --> 00:02:22.600
Hey, conscience, am I dead?

38
00:02:22.684 --> 00:02:24.185
I see it, too.

39
00:02:31.735 --> 00:02:33.152
What is it?

40
00:02:33.946 --> 00:02:36.614
It's so pretty!

41
00:02:38.533 --> 00:02:39.951
I...

42
00:02:40.035 --> 00:02:42.286
I'm feeling happy.

43
00:02:43.455 --> 00:02:46.749
Which is a big deal for me.

44
00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:48.584
I want to touch it.

45
00:02:49.878 --> 00:02:52.255
Hey, come back.
Come on back here.

46
00:02:52.339 --> 00:02:56.133
I'm going to get you.

47
00:02:56.218 --> 00:02:58.052
I'm going to swim with you

48
00:02:58.136 --> 00:03:00.888
I'm going to be
your best friend

49
00:03:00.973 --> 00:03:02.306
Good feeling's gone.

50
00:03:09.731 --> 00:03:11.857
I can't see. I don't
know where I'm going.

51
00:03:13.902 --> 00:03:15.820
- The mask!
- What mask?

52
00:03:16.989 --> 00:03:19.073
Okay. I can't see a thing.

53
00:03:19.825 --> 00:03:20.866
Whoa, geez.

54
00:03:20.951 --> 00:03:22.994
- Look. A mask.
- Read it!

55
00:03:24.162 --> 00:03:28.082
I'm sorry, but if you could bring it
a little closer. I need the light.

56
00:03:28.166 --> 00:03:30.251
That's great. Keep
it right there.

57
00:03:30.335 --> 00:03:33.170
- Just read it!
- Okay, okay.

58
00:03:33.255 --> 00:03:34.714
Mr. Bossy.

59
00:03:35.549 --> 00:03:37.258
"P." Okay. P.

60
00:03:37.342 --> 00:03:38.926
"Sher..."

61
00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.595
P. Sher... P. Shirley...

62
00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:43.180
P not Shirley.

63
00:03:44.391 --> 00:03:46.267
The first line's "P. Sherman."

64
00:03:46.351 --> 00:03:48.936
"P. Sherman" doesn't
make any sense!

65
00:03:49.021 --> 00:03:50.396
Second line.

66
00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:52.023
"42..."

67
00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.819
Light, please.

68
00:03:56.903 --> 00:04:00.531
"Walla... Wallaby."

69
00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:05.619
The second line's
"42 Wallaby Way."

70
00:04:05.704 --> 00:04:08.789
Just finish up. Speed read.
No pressure.

71
00:04:08.874 --> 00:04:11.876
There's a lot of pressure!
Take a guess, with pressure.

72
00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:14.378
- Sydney. It's Sydney!
- Duck!

73
00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:20.509
I'm dead. I'm dead.

74
00:04:20.594 --> 00:04:22.386
I died. I'm dead.

75
00:04:29.186 --> 00:04:30.186
Whoo-hoo!

76
00:04:30.729 --> 00:04:32.313
We did it, we did it

77
00:04:32.397 --> 00:04:34.065
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah

78
00:04:34.149 --> 00:04:37.318
No eating here tonight,
eating here tonight

79
00:04:37.402 --> 00:04:40.154
No eating here tonight
You're on a diet

80
00:04:40.238 --> 00:04:43.115
Dory. What did it say?
What did the mask say?

81
00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.743
P. Sherman,
42 Wallaby Way, Sydney.

82
00:04:45.827 --> 00:04:49.205
I remembered what it said! I forget
things, but I remembered it.

83
00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:51.332
- P. Sherman...
- Where is that?

84
00:04:51.416 --> 00:04:53.959
I don't know. But who cares?
I remembered.

85
00:04:55.504 --> 00:04:59.131
P. Sherman, 42 Wallaby Way,
Sydney. I remembered it again!

86
00:05:26.243 --> 00:05:27.493
Psst!

87
00:05:28.412 --> 00:05:29.829
Nemo.

88
00:05:30.789 --> 00:05:32.498
Nemo!

89
00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:34.750
Huh?

90
00:05:34.835 --> 00:05:35.835
Suivez-moi.

91
00:05:38.296 --> 00:05:39.755
Follow me.

92
00:06:34.394 --> 00:06:35.394
Hoo!

93
00:06:37.689 --> 00:06:39.023
State your name.

94
00:06:40.025 --> 00:06:41.108
Nemo.

95
00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:43.569
Brother Bloat, proceed.

96
00:06:45.197 --> 00:06:48.574
Nemo, newcomer of
orange and white.

97
00:06:48.825 --> 00:06:53.078
You have been called forth to the
summit of Mount Wannahockaloogie

98
00:06:53.163 --> 00:06:57.875
to join with us in the
fraternal bonds of tankhood.

99
00:06:58.543 --> 00:06:59.543
Huh?

100
00:06:59.586 --> 00:07:01.962
- We want you in our club, kid.
- Really?

101
00:07:02.047 --> 00:07:05.799
If you are able to swim through

102
00:07:05.884 --> 00:07:09.386
the Ring of Fire!

103
00:07:13.475 --> 00:07:16.852
Turn on the Ring of Fire.
You said you could do it.

104
00:07:16.937 --> 00:07:18.729
The Ring of Fire!

105
00:07:21.107 --> 00:07:22.983
Bubbles. Let me...

106
00:07:30.825 --> 00:07:33.661
Isn't there another way?
He's just a boy.

107
00:07:44.839 --> 00:07:49.134
From this moment on, you will
now be known as Sharkbait.

108
00:07:49.219 --> 00:07:50.511
Sharkbait! Oo-ha-ha!

109
00:07:50.595 --> 00:07:52.304
Welcome, Brother Sharkbait.

110
00:07:52.389 --> 00:07:53.597
Sharkbait.

111
00:07:53.682 --> 00:07:56.433
- Enough with the Sharkbait.
- Sharkbait, oo...

112
00:07:57.602 --> 00:07:59.853
- Sharkbait's one of us now.
- Agreed.

113
00:07:59.938 --> 00:08:03.357
We can't send him to his death.
Darla's coming in five days.

114
00:08:03.441 --> 00:08:04.942
So what are we going to do?

115
00:08:06.194 --> 00:08:07.903
I'll tell you.

116
00:08:07.988 --> 00:08:10.698
We're going to get him out of
here. We'll help him escape.

117
00:08:10.782 --> 00:08:13.242
- Escape? Really?
- We're all going to escape.

118
00:08:13.535 --> 00:08:15.911
Not another one of
your escape plans.

119
00:08:15.996 --> 00:08:18.038
Sorry, but they never work.

120
00:08:18.123 --> 00:08:19.684
Yeah, why should this
be any different?

121
00:08:20.083 --> 00:08:23.043
- 'Cause we've got him.
- Me?

122
00:08:23.128 --> 00:08:24.795
- You see that filter?
- Yeah.

123
00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:28.591
You're the only one who can
get in and out of that thing.

124
00:08:28.675 --> 00:08:32.886
We need you to take a pebble
inside there and jam the gears.

125
00:08:32.971 --> 00:08:36.765
You do that and this tank's going
to get filthier by the minute.

126
00:08:36.850 --> 00:08:39.518
Soon the dentist will
have to clean the tank.

127
00:08:39.603 --> 00:08:43.731
When he does, he'll take us out of the
tank, put us in individual baggies,

128
00:08:43.815 --> 00:08:46.734
then we'll roll down the
counter, out of the window,

129
00:08:46.818 --> 00:08:50.321
off the awning, into the bushes, across
the street and into the harbour.

130
00:08:51.573 --> 00:08:52.990
It's foolproof.

131
00:08:53.533 --> 00:08:56.076
- Who's with me?
- I.

132
00:08:56.161 --> 00:08:57.995
- I think you're nuts.

133
00:08:58.371 --> 00:09:01.332
No of fence, kid, but you're
not the best swimmer.

134
00:09:01.416 --> 00:09:04.168
He's fine. He can do this.

135
00:09:04.252 --> 00:09:07.379
So, Sharkbait,
what do you think?

136
00:09:07.464 --> 00:09:08.672
Let's do it!

137
00:09:13.261 --> 00:09:16.388
P. Sherman, 42 Wallaby Way,
Sydney. Where are you going?

138
00:09:16.473 --> 00:09:18.766
To P. Sherman, 42
Wallaby Way, Sydney.

139
00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:21.185
If you ask where I'm
going, I'll tell you.

140
00:09:21.269 --> 00:09:26.607
P. Sherman, 42 Wallaby Way, Sydney.
Where? I'm sorry. I didn't hear you.

141
00:09:26.691 --> 00:09:29.902
Excuse me. Excuse me.

142
00:09:29.986 --> 00:09:32.321
Hi. Do you know how to get...
Hello?

143
00:09:32.405 --> 00:09:35.157
Wait. Can you tell me... Hey!

144
00:09:35.241 --> 00:09:36.617
Hold it!

145
00:09:36.701 --> 00:09:38.661
Wait a minute. I'm
trying to talk to you.

146
00:09:39.454 --> 00:09:41.288
Okay, fellas. Come back here.

147
00:09:41.373 --> 00:09:45.209
One quick question. I need to...
And they're gone again.

148
00:09:46.211 --> 00:09:48.629
P. Sherman, 42
Wallaby Way, Sydney.

149
00:09:48.713 --> 00:09:50.881
Why do I have to tell you again?

150
00:09:50.965 --> 00:09:54.468
- I don't get tired of it.
- All right, here's the thing.

151
00:09:55.387 --> 00:09:59.765
I think it's best if I
carry on from here by...

152
00:10:00.934 --> 00:10:03.227
- By myself.
- Okay.

153
00:10:03.311 --> 00:10:04.853
You know. Alone.

154
00:10:04.938 --> 00:10:09.858
Without... Well, not without you,
but I don't want you with me.

155
00:10:11.611 --> 00:10:14.029
- Huh? - I don't want
to hurt your feelings.

156
00:10:14.114 --> 00:10:16.824
- You want me to leave?
- Well, not... Yes. Yeah.

157
00:10:16.908 --> 00:10:19.493
I just can't afford
any more delays.

158
00:10:19.577 --> 00:10:22.454
You're one of those fish
that 'cause delays.

159
00:10:22.539 --> 00:10:25.582
Sometimes it's a good thing.
There's a group of fish.

160
00:10:25.667 --> 00:10:28.127
- They're delay fish.
- You mean...

161
00:10:28.962 --> 00:10:32.464
- You mean you don't like me?
- Of course I like you.

162
00:10:32.549 --> 00:10:35.008
Because I like you I don't
want to be with you.

163
00:10:35.093 --> 00:10:37.261
It's a complicated emotion.

164
00:10:38.763 --> 00:10:41.098
Don't cry. I like you.

165
00:10:41.182 --> 00:10:42.307
Hey, you!

166
00:10:43.059 --> 00:10:45.394
Lady, is this guy bothering you?

167
00:10:45.478 --> 00:10:49.398
- I don't remember. Were you?
- No, no. We're just...

168
00:10:49.482 --> 00:10:51.358
Do you guys know
how I can get...

169
00:10:51.443 --> 00:10:55.154
We're talking to the lady, not
you. You like impressions?

170
00:10:55.739 --> 00:10:56.739
Mmm-hmm.

171
00:10:56.823 --> 00:10:59.742
Okay. Just like in
rehearsals, gentlemen.

172
00:10:59.826 --> 00:11:01.535
What are we? Take a guess.

173
00:11:01.619 --> 00:11:04.663
- I've seen one of those. - I'm
a fish with a nose like a sword.

174
00:11:04.789 --> 00:11:06.707
- Wait.
- It's a swordfish.

175
00:11:06.791 --> 00:11:09.376
Hey, clown-boy, let
the lady guess.

176
00:11:10.086 --> 00:11:11.378
Where's the butter?

177
00:11:11.921 --> 00:11:13.714
- It's on the tip of my tongue.
- Lobster.

178
00:11:13.798 --> 00:11:15.215
- Saw that.
- What?

179
00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:17.342
- Lots of legs.
- Clam?

180
00:11:17.427 --> 00:11:18.635
Close enough.

181
00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:21.180
It's a whale of a tale
I'll tell you, lad

182
00:11:21.264 --> 00:11:23.515
- They're good.
- Somebody give me directions?

183
00:11:24.267 --> 00:11:27.394
- "Would somebody give me directions?"

184
00:11:27.479 --> 00:11:29.813
- I'm serious.
- Blah, blah, me, me.

185
00:11:29.898 --> 00:11:31.356
Blah, blah, blah, me, me.

186
00:11:31.441 --> 00:11:33.025
Thank you.

187
00:11:33.109 --> 00:11:35.319
Oh, dear. Hey, come back.

188
00:11:36.237 --> 00:11:38.238
What's the matter?

189
00:11:38.323 --> 00:11:40.449
While they're doing impressions,

190
00:11:40.533 --> 00:11:42.075
I am miles from home

191
00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:44.203
with a fish that can't even
remember her own name.

192
00:11:44.412 --> 00:11:47.039
- I bet that's frustrating.
- My son is out there.

193
00:11:47.123 --> 00:11:49.041
- Your son Chico?
- Nemo.

194
00:11:49.125 --> 00:11:52.753
It doesn't matter. 'Cause no fish
in this ocean is going to help me.

195
00:11:52.837 --> 00:11:54.505
I'm helping you.

196
00:11:56.466 --> 00:11:58.175
Wait right here.

197
00:11:59.511 --> 00:12:01.595
- Guys.
- Is he bothering you again?

198
00:12:01.679 --> 00:12:03.263
No, he's a good guy.

199
00:12:03.348 --> 00:12:05.724
Go easy on him. He's
lost his son Fabio.

200
00:12:05.809 --> 00:12:08.310
Heard of P. Sherman, 42
Wallaby Way, Sydney?

201
00:12:08.394 --> 00:12:10.771
Sydney? Oh, sure.

202
00:12:10.855 --> 00:12:13.774
Ted here's got relatives
in Sydney. Don't you, Ted?

203
00:12:13.858 --> 00:12:17.236
- Sure do.
- Hey, they know Sydney!

204
00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:20.948
- You wouldn't know how to get there?
- Follow the EAC.

205
00:12:21.032 --> 00:12:23.617
That's East Australian Current.

206
00:12:23.701 --> 00:12:26.787
Big current. You can't Miss it.
It's in

207
00:12:26.871 --> 00:12:28.330
that direction.

208
00:12:28.414 --> 00:12:30.958
Then you got to follow
that for about...

209
00:12:31.042 --> 00:12:33.794
What do you guys think?
Three leagues?

210
00:12:33.878 --> 00:12:36.964
That baby's going to float
you right past Sydney.

211
00:12:37.048 --> 00:12:38.549
Great! That's great!

212
00:12:38.633 --> 00:12:40.676
- Dory, you did it.
- Oh, please.

213
00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:42.970
I'm just your little helper.
Helping along.

214
00:12:43.054 --> 00:12:45.305
- Fellas, thank you.
- Don't mention it.

215
00:12:45.390 --> 00:12:47.850
Just loosen up. Okay, buddy?

216
00:12:47.934 --> 00:12:51.019
You guys! You really nailed him.
Bye.

217
00:12:51.104 --> 00:12:52.688
- Ma'am. One more thing.
- Yes?

218
00:12:52.772 --> 00:12:56.400
When you come to this trench,
swim through it, not over it.

219
00:12:56.484 --> 00:12:59.570
Trench. Through it. Not over it.
I'll remember.

220
00:12:59.654 --> 00:13:00.904
Hey!

221
00:13:03.157 --> 00:13:04.616
Wait up, partner. Hold on.

222
00:13:05.243 --> 00:13:08.537
Wait. I've got to tell
you something. Whoa.

223
00:13:10.373 --> 00:13:12.207
Nice trench.

224
00:13:14.586 --> 00:13:16.670
Hello!

225
00:13:20.341 --> 00:13:22.843
- Let's go. - No, no.
- Bad trench. Bad trench.

226
00:13:22.927 --> 00:13:26.889
- We're going to swim over this thing.
- Little red flag going up.

227
00:13:26.973 --> 00:13:30.017
Something's telling me we
should swim through it.

228
00:13:30.101 --> 00:13:33.228
Are you looking at this thing?
It's got death written on it.

229
00:13:33.313 --> 00:13:36.106
I'm sorry, but I think
we should swim through.

230
00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:38.317
I'm done talking about this.
Over we go.

231
00:13:38.401 --> 00:13:39.818
Come on. Trust me on this.

232
00:13:39.903 --> 00:13:42.279
- Trust you? - Yes. Trust.
- It's what friends do.

233
00:13:43.156 --> 00:13:44.781
- Something shiny!
- Where?

234
00:13:44.866 --> 00:13:47.826
- It just swam over the trench. Come on.
- Okay.

235
00:13:52.957 --> 00:13:55.792
- Boy, it sure is clear up here.
- Exactly.

236
00:13:55.877 --> 00:13:57.085
And look at that.

237
00:13:57.170 --> 00:14:00.464
There's the current. We
should be there in no time.

238
00:14:00.924 --> 00:14:04.051
- Hey, little guy. - You wanted
to go through the trench.

239
00:14:04.135 --> 00:14:08.555
I shall call him Squishy and he
shall be mine. Come here, Squishy.

240
00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:10.682
Come here, little Squishy.

241
00:14:12.518 --> 00:14:13.518
Ow!

242
00:14:13.645 --> 00:14:16.772
- That's a jellyfish!
- Bad Squishy.

243
00:14:16.856 --> 00:14:18.231
Shoo! Get away.

244
00:14:18.316 --> 00:14:20.192
- Let me see.
- Don't touch it.

245
00:14:20.276 --> 00:14:22.736
I'm not going to touch it.
I just want to look.

246
00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:24.696
How come it didn't sting you?

247
00:14:24.781 --> 00:14:27.240
It did. Hold still.

248
00:14:28.076 --> 00:14:32.579
I live in this anemone and I'm used
to these kind of stings. Come here.

249
00:14:32.664 --> 00:14:34.706
You're going to be fine.

250
00:14:34.791 --> 00:14:38.085
But now we know that we don't
want to touch these again.

251
00:14:38.169 --> 00:14:40.712
Let's be thankful it
was just a little one.

252
00:14:44.175 --> 00:14:45.342
Don't move.

253
00:14:47.512 --> 00:14:49.471
This is bad, Dory.

254
00:14:50.264 --> 00:14:53.725
- Boing. Boing.
- Dory!

255
00:14:53.810 --> 00:14:55.477
You can't catch me.

256
00:14:55.561 --> 00:14:58.188
Don't bounce on the tops.
They will

257
00:14:58.272 --> 00:15:00.107
not sting you!

258
00:15:00.191 --> 00:15:03.527
- The tops don't sting you.
- Two in a row. Beat that.

259
00:15:03.611 --> 00:15:05.237
Listen to me. I have an idea.

260
00:15:05.321 --> 00:15:07.114
- A game.
- A game?

261
00:15:07.198 --> 00:15:08.865
I love games. Pick me.

262
00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:13.495
Here's the game. Whoever can hop the
fastest out of these jellyfish wins.

263
00:15:13.579 --> 00:15:15.122
- Okay!
- Rules.

264
00:15:15.206 --> 00:15:17.708
Don't touch the tentacles.
Only the tops.

265
00:15:17.792 --> 00:15:21.378
Something about tentacles. Got
it. On your Mark. Get set. Go!

266
00:15:22.714 --> 00:15:24.256
Wait!

267
00:15:24.340 --> 00:15:26.383
Go faster if you want to win.

268
00:15:26.467 --> 00:15:28.885
- Dory!
- Boing, boing, boing!

269
00:15:29.846 --> 00:15:31.930
Wait a minute.

270
00:15:32.432 --> 00:15:33.432
Whee!

271
00:15:34.350 --> 00:15:36.143
So, we're cheating death now.

272
00:15:36.227 --> 00:15:38.812
We're having fun
at the same time.

273
00:15:38.896 --> 00:15:40.605
I can do this. Just be careful.

274
00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:42.357
Careful I don't make
you cry when I win.

275
00:15:42.442 --> 00:15:43.900
I don't think so!

276
00:15:47.196 --> 00:15:50.574
Give it up. You can't fight
evolution. I was built for speed.

277
00:15:50.658 --> 00:15:53.118
- The question is, are you hungry?
- Hungry?

278
00:15:53.202 --> 00:15:55.704
Yeah. 'Cause you're about
to eat my bubbles!

279
00:15:56.372 --> 00:15:59.332
Duck to the left, back and
coming over, right there!

280
00:16:01.419 --> 00:16:04.212
The clownfish is the winner!

281
00:16:04.297 --> 00:16:06.757
We did it. Look at us!

282
00:16:06.841 --> 00:16:08.091
Dory?

283
00:16:10.595 --> 00:16:11.595
Oh, no.

284
00:16:13.097 --> 00:16:16.892
Dory! Dory! Dory!

285
00:16:19.771 --> 00:16:21.354
Dory!

286
00:16:23.816 --> 00:16:24.816
Aagghh!

287
00:16:26.903 --> 00:16:28.361
Am I disqualified?

288
00:16:28.446 --> 00:16:30.530
You're doing fine.
You're winning.

289
00:16:30.615 --> 00:16:33.366
Stay awake. Where does P.
Sherman live?

290
00:16:33.451 --> 00:16:36.620
P. Sherman, Wallaby Way, Sydney.

291
00:16:36.704 --> 00:16:38.163
That's it!

292
00:16:41.542 --> 00:16:44.461
Stay awake. Stay awake.
Stay awake.

293
00:16:44.796 --> 00:16:47.756
Stay awake!

294
00:16:51.469 --> 00:16:53.887
- Awake...
- P. Sherman...

295
00:16:54.555 --> 00:16:57.099
- Awake...
- 42 Wallaby Way...

296
00:16:57.934 --> 00:16:59.851
- Wake up.
- Sydney.

297
00:16:59.936 --> 00:17:00.977
Nemo...

298
00:17:16.285 --> 00:17:18.537
You Miss your dad,
don't you, Sharkbait?

299
00:17:18.621 --> 00:17:19.746
Yeah.

300
00:17:19.831 --> 00:17:23.708
Well, you're lucky to have someone
out there who's looking for you.

301
00:17:23.793 --> 00:17:25.961
He's not looking for me.

302
00:17:26.045 --> 00:17:28.130
He's scared of the ocean.

303
00:17:29.674 --> 00:17:31.007
Peach? Any movement?

304
00:17:31.092 --> 00:17:33.760
He's had four cups of coffee.
It's got to be soon.

305
00:17:34.011 --> 00:17:35.512
Keep on him.

306
00:17:38.182 --> 00:17:40.976
My first escape, landed
on dental tools.

307
00:17:41.060 --> 00:17:43.436
- I was aiming for the toilet.
- The toilet?

308
00:17:43.521 --> 00:17:46.398
All drains lead to
the ocean, kid.

309
00:17:46.482 --> 00:17:49.484
Wow. How many times have
you tried to get out?

310
00:17:49.569 --> 00:17:54.614
I've lost count. Fish aren't meant to be
in a box, kid. It does things to you.

311
00:17:54.699 --> 00:17:56.783
The bubbles, the bubbles!

312
00:17:56.868 --> 00:18:00.954
Potty break! He just grabbed the
Reader's Digest. We have 4.2 minutes.

313
00:18:01.038 --> 00:18:02.622
That's your cue.

314
00:18:02.707 --> 00:18:05.083
- You can do it, kid.
- We got to be quick.

315
00:18:05.168 --> 00:18:09.462
Once you get in, swim to the bottom
and I'll talk you through the rest.

316
00:18:09.547 --> 00:18:10.547
Okay.

317
00:18:10.631 --> 00:18:13.008
- Go on. It'll be a piece of kelp.

318
00:18:21.184 --> 00:18:23.810
- Nicely done. Can you hear me?
- Yeah.

319
00:18:23.895 --> 00:18:25.812
Here comes the pebble.

320
00:18:31.986 --> 00:18:35.530
- Now, do you see a small opening?
- Uh-huh.

321
00:18:35.615 --> 00:18:38.742
Okay. Inside it you'll
see a rotating fan.

322
00:18:38.826 --> 00:18:43.246
Very carefully, wedge that pebble
into the fan to stop it turning.

323
00:18:47.793 --> 00:18:49.169
Careful, Sharkbait.

324
00:18:49.253 --> 00:18:51.922
- I can't do it.
- This isn't a good idea.

325
00:18:52.006 --> 00:18:53.715
He'll be fine. Try again!

326
00:18:54.008 --> 00:18:55.383
Okay.

327
00:18:56.427 --> 00:18:59.137
That's it, Sharkbait.

328
00:18:59.222 --> 00:19:01.473
Nice and steady.

329
00:19:04.018 --> 00:19:06.937
- I got it, I got it!
- He did it.

330
00:19:07.021 --> 00:19:10.232
That's great, kid. Now
swim up the tube and out.

331
00:19:27.792 --> 00:19:29.793
Oh, no! Gill!

332
00:19:30.503 --> 00:19:32.796
Sharkbait! Get him out of there!

333
00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:34.381
- Help him!
- What do we do?

334
00:19:34.465 --> 00:19:37.342
- Oh, no! - Stay calm,
kid. Just don't panic.

335
00:19:38.844 --> 00:19:42.013
- Help me!
- Sharkbait, grab hold of this.

336
00:19:45.726 --> 00:19:46.726
No!

337
00:19:46.811 --> 00:19:48.728
- Feed me more.
- That's it!

338
00:19:48.813 --> 00:19:50.939
Come on, Sharkbait. Grab it.

339
00:19:52.566 --> 00:19:54.526
- I got it.
- Pull!

340
00:20:02.326 --> 00:20:04.661
Gill, don't make him
go back in there.

341
00:20:06.163 --> 00:20:09.499
No. We're done.

342
00:20:23.597 --> 00:20:25.098
Dude?

343
00:20:26.392 --> 00:20:27.726
Dude?

344
00:20:28.519 --> 00:20:30.312
Focus, dude.

345
00:20:31.105 --> 00:20:32.355
Dude?

346
00:20:34.108 --> 00:20:35.650
He lives. Hey, dude.

347
00:20:38.404 --> 00:20:41.364
- What happened?
- I saw the whole thing, dude.

348
00:20:41.449 --> 00:20:44.868
First you were all, like, whoa!
And then we were all, like, whoa!

349
00:20:44.952 --> 00:20:48.163
- Then you were, like, whoa...
- What are you talking about?

350
00:20:48.247 --> 00:20:55.128
You, mini-man! Taking on the jellies.
You got serious thrill issues, dude.

351
00:20:55.212 --> 00:20:56.421
Awesome.

352
00:20:56.881 --> 00:20:58.381
Oh, my stomach.

353
00:20:59.133 --> 00:21:02.260
Man, no hurling on the shell.
I just waxed it.

354
00:21:03.512 --> 00:21:06.806
- So, Mr. Turtle...
- Dude, Mr. Turtle is my father.

355
00:21:06.891 --> 00:21:08.391
Name's Crush.

356
00:21:08.726 --> 00:21:10.477
Crush? Really?

357
00:21:11.062 --> 00:21:12.312
Okay, Crush.

358
00:21:12.396 --> 00:21:15.774
Listen, I need to get to the
East Australian Current.

359
00:21:15.858 --> 00:21:17.317
EAC?

360
00:21:17.401 --> 00:21:18.943
Dude...

361
00:21:19.028 --> 00:21:21.196
You're riding it, dude.

362
00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:23.073
Check it out.

363
00:21:45.054 --> 00:21:46.554
Okay, grab shell, dude.

364
00:21:46.639 --> 00:21:48.848
Grab what?

365
00:21:58.609 --> 00:22:00.360
Righteous! Righteous!

366
00:22:05.366 --> 00:22:06.825
So,

367
00:22:07.660 --> 00:22:11.413
what brings you on this
fine day to the EAC?

368
00:22:11.497 --> 00:22:14.499
Well, Dory and I need
to get to Sydney.

369
00:22:14.583 --> 00:22:16.793
Dory! Is she all right?

370
00:22:17.253 --> 00:22:19.421
Oh, little blue.

371
00:22:19.505 --> 00:22:20.672
She is sub-level, dude.

372
00:22:24.927 --> 00:22:26.886
Dory, Dory! Dory!

373
00:22:27.847 --> 00:22:29.055
Oh, Dory.

374
00:22:32.017 --> 00:22:33.643
I'm so sorry.

375
00:22:34.311 --> 00:22:37.188
This is all my fault.
It's my fault.

376
00:22:37.273 --> 00:22:40.275
Twenty-nine, 30! Ready
or not, here I come!

377
00:22:42.987 --> 00:22:44.112
There you are.

378
00:22:44.822 --> 00:22:46.322
Catch me if you can.

379
00:22:56.333 --> 00:22:58.126
Up you go!

380
00:23:08.637 --> 00:23:09.929
Oh, my goodness.

381
00:23:10.014 --> 00:23:14.100
Kill the motor, dude. Let us see
what Squirt does flying solo.

382
00:23:22.943 --> 00:23:25.737
Whoa! That was so cool.

383
00:23:25.821 --> 00:23:28.615
Hey, Dad. Did you see that?
Did you see me?

384
00:23:28.699 --> 00:23:32.869
- Did you see what I did?
- You so totally rock, Squirt.

385
00:23:32.953 --> 00:23:34.621
Give me some fin.

386
00:23:34.705 --> 00:23:35.788
Noggin.

387
00:23:35.873 --> 00:23:37.207
Dude.

388
00:23:38.042 --> 00:23:42.712
Intro. Jellyman, Offspring.
Offspring, Jellyman.

389
00:23:42.796 --> 00:23:46.257
- Jellies? Sweet.
- Totally.

390
00:23:46.342 --> 00:23:49.552
I must have done something
you all liked, dudes.

391
00:23:49.637 --> 00:23:51.763
- You rock, dude.
- Ow.

392
00:23:52.681 --> 00:23:54.849
Curl away, my son.

393
00:23:54.934 --> 00:23:56.809
It's awesome, Jellyman.

394
00:23:56.894 --> 00:24:00.271
When the little dudes are eggs we
leave them on a beach to hatch,

395
00:24:00.564 --> 00:24:04.317
and coo-coo-cachoo, they find their
way back to the big ol' blue.

396
00:24:04.401 --> 00:24:06.486
- All by themselves?
- Yeah!

397
00:24:06.570 --> 00:24:09.489
But, dude, how do you
know when they're ready?

398
00:24:09.573 --> 00:24:13.743
You never really know, but when
they know, you'll know. You know?

399
00:24:18.624 --> 00:24:21.167
- Hey, look, everybody.
- I know that dude.

400
00:24:21.252 --> 00:24:22.544
It's the Jellyman.

401
00:24:23.254 --> 00:24:26.047
- Well go on. Jump on him.
- Turtle pile!

402
00:24:26.131 --> 00:24:27.840
Wait. Kids!

403
00:24:27.925 --> 00:24:29.801
- You funny?
- Where's your shell?

404
00:24:29.885 --> 00:24:32.178
- Do your stripes come off?
- I need to breathe.

405
00:24:32.263 --> 00:24:34.472
Did you cross the
jellyfish Forest?

406
00:24:34.557 --> 00:24:37.559
- One at a time.
- Mr. Fish, did you die?

407
00:24:37.643 --> 00:24:39.769
Sorry. I was vague
on the details.

408
00:24:39.853 --> 00:24:43.356
- So where are you going?
- You see, my son was taken.

409
00:24:43.440 --> 00:24:45.692
My son was taken away from me.

410
00:24:46.569 --> 00:24:48.486
- No way!
- What happened?

411
00:24:48.571 --> 00:24:51.531
No, kids. I don't want
to talk about it.

412
00:24:51.615 --> 00:24:54.117
- Come on.
- Please.

413
00:24:55.536 --> 00:24:56.536
Well, okay.

414
00:24:57.329 --> 00:25:00.832
I live on this reef, a
long way from here.

415
00:25:01.083 --> 00:25:03.167
This is going to be good.
I can tell.

416
00:25:03.252 --> 00:25:07.380
My son, Nemo, he was mad at me.

417
00:25:08.132 --> 00:25:10.800
Maybe he wouldn't have done it if
I hadn't been so tough on him.

418
00:25:10.884 --> 00:25:12.218
I don't know.

419
00:25:12.303 --> 00:25:14.721
He swam in the open
water to this boat

420
00:25:14.805 --> 00:25:18.266
and these divers appeared
and I tried to stop them.

421
00:25:18.350 --> 00:25:21.227
The boat was too fast, so
we swam out in the ocean...

422
00:25:21.312 --> 00:25:22.478
He couldn't stop them.

423
00:25:22.563 --> 00:25:25.356
Then Nemo's dad, he
swims out to the ocean

424
00:25:25.441 --> 00:25:27.692
and they bump into three sharks.

425
00:25:27.776 --> 00:25:30.194
He scares them away
by blowing them up.

426
00:25:30.279 --> 00:25:32.989
- That's amazing. - Then
dives thousands of feet...

427
00:25:33.073 --> 00:25:37.243
Straight into the dark. It's wicked
dark there. You can't see a thing.

428
00:25:37.328 --> 00:25:39.787
The only thing they can
see down there is...

429
00:25:39.872 --> 00:25:43.583
This big, horrible creature with
razor-sharp teeth! Nice parry.

430
00:25:43.667 --> 00:25:45.168
Then he has to blast his way...

431
00:25:45.252 --> 00:25:48.212
These fish have been
searching the ocean for days

432
00:25:48.297 --> 00:25:50.089
on the East Australian Current.

433
00:25:50.174 --> 00:25:52.216
He may be on his way
here right now.

434
00:25:52.301 --> 00:25:53.926
That should put him
in Sydney Harbour...

435
00:25:54.011 --> 00:25:55.386
In a few days.

436
00:25:55.471 --> 00:25:57.430
This guy will stop at nothing...

437
00:25:57.514 --> 00:26:00.308
stop at nothing until he finds
his son. I hope he makes it.

438
00:26:00.392 --> 00:26:03.227
That's one dedicated
father, if you ask me.

439
00:26:09.860 --> 00:26:12.362
Mine. Mine. Mine.

440
00:26:18.494 --> 00:26:21.204
Would you just shut up?

441
00:26:21.288 --> 00:26:25.083
- You're rats with wings. - This
bloke's looking for his boy, Nemo.

442
00:26:25.167 --> 00:26:28.836
- He was taken off the reef by divers...
- There. Take it.

443
00:26:29.880 --> 00:26:32.465
Say that again. You said
something about Nemo.

444
00:26:32.549 --> 00:26:34.258
Mine. Mine. Mine.

445
00:26:37.054 --> 00:26:38.054
Mine.

446
00:26:38.138 --> 00:26:41.307
Last I heard, he's heading
towards the harbour.

447
00:26:41.392 --> 00:26:42.725
Brilliant!

448
00:26:56.532 --> 00:26:57.907
Is he doing okay?

449
00:26:57.991 --> 00:27:01.244
I don't know, but whatever you
do, don't mention D-A-R...

450
00:27:01.328 --> 00:27:04.372
It's okay. I know who
you're talking about.

451
00:27:12.673 --> 00:27:13.673
Gill?

452
00:27:18.887 --> 00:27:20.096
Hey, Sharkbait.

453
00:27:21.140 --> 00:27:24.559
- I'm sorry I couldn't stop... - I'm the one who should be sorry.

454
00:27:25.853 --> 00:27:30.064
I was so ready to get out, so
ready to taste that ocean,

455
00:27:30.691 --> 00:27:33.443
I was willing to put you in
harm's way to get there.

456
00:27:34.737 --> 00:27:36.946
Nothing should be worth that.

457
00:27:38.449 --> 00:27:40.783
I'm sorry I couldn't get you
back to your father, kid.

458
00:27:45.080 --> 00:27:47.081
All right. Hey, hey, hey!

459
00:27:47.833 --> 00:27:49.292
- What the...
- Aaggh!

460
00:27:49.376 --> 00:27:52.962
Well, that's one way
to pull a tooth.

461
00:27:54.465 --> 00:27:58.468
Darn kids. Well, good thing
I pulled the right one, eh?

462
00:27:58.802 --> 00:27:59.802
Pssst!

463
00:27:59.887 --> 00:28:02.013
Nigel, you just
missed an extraction.

464
00:28:02.097 --> 00:28:04.807
Has he loosened the
periodontal ligament yet?

465
00:28:04.892 --> 00:28:07.059
What am I talking about?
Where's Nemo?

466
00:28:07.144 --> 00:28:08.770
I've got to speak with him.

467
00:28:08.854 --> 00:28:11.898
Your dad's been fighting
the ocean looking for you.

468
00:28:11.982 --> 00:28:13.983
My father? Really?

469
00:28:14.067 --> 00:28:15.902
He's travelled
hundreds of miles.

470
00:28:15.986 --> 00:28:19.197
- He's been battling sharks and jellyfish.
- Sharks?

471
00:28:19.281 --> 00:28:22.200
- That can't be him. - Are
you sure? What was his name?

472
00:28:22.284 --> 00:28:24.285
Some sort of sport fish.
Tuna? Trout?

473
00:28:24.369 --> 00:28:25.953
- Marlin?
- That's it.

474
00:28:26.038 --> 00:28:29.624
- The clownfish from the reef.
- It's my dad! He took on a shark!

475
00:28:29.708 --> 00:28:32.710
- I heard he took on three.
- Three?

476
00:28:32.795 --> 00:28:35.087
- Three sharks?
- That's 4,800 teeth!

477
00:28:35.172 --> 00:28:37.340
After you were taken
by Diver Dan,

478
00:28:37.424 --> 00:28:39.425
your dad followed the
boat like a maniac.

479
00:28:39.510 --> 00:28:40.676
Really?

480
00:28:40.761 --> 00:28:44.347
He's giving it all he's got and
then three sharks capture him.

481
00:28:44.431 --> 00:28:47.225
He blows 'em up and then
dives thousands of feet

482
00:28:47.309 --> 00:28:49.769
and gets chased by a
monster with huge teeth!

483
00:28:49.853 --> 00:28:52.396
He ties this demon to a rock.
And his reward?

484
00:28:52.481 --> 00:28:54.857
He gets to battle a
jellyfish Forest.

485
00:28:54.942 --> 00:28:58.069
Now he's with sea turtles on
the East Australian Current

486
00:28:58.153 --> 00:29:01.614
and the word is he's headed
this way, right now, to Sydney!

487
00:29:02.115 --> 00:29:05.701
- What a good daddy. - He was
looking for you after all.

488
00:29:09.498 --> 00:29:12.291
- He's swimming in the filter!
- Not again!

489
00:29:14.545 --> 00:29:15.545
Sharkbait!

490
00:29:17.631 --> 00:29:19.882
- No! - You've got your
life ahead of you.

491
00:29:19.967 --> 00:29:21.884
- We'll help you.
- Get him out.

492
00:29:27.599 --> 00:29:30.184
- Get him out of there.
- Come on. Grab the end.

493
00:29:31.687 --> 00:29:33.229
Are you okay?

494
00:29:33.313 --> 00:29:36.315
Can you hear me, Sharkbait?
Nemo? Can you hear me?

495
00:29:36.400 --> 00:29:37.859
Yeah, I can hear you.

496
00:29:38.527 --> 00:29:40.570
Sharkbait, you did it!

497
00:29:40.654 --> 00:29:43.573
Sharkbait, you're...
Covered with germs!

498
00:29:44.074 --> 00:29:45.533
That took guts.

499
00:29:46.285 --> 00:29:49.787
All right, we have less than 48
hours before Darla gets here.

500
00:29:49.872 --> 00:29:51.914
This tank will get plenty
dirty in that time,

501
00:29:51.999 --> 00:29:54.166
but we have to help it along.

502
00:29:54.251 --> 00:29:56.711
- Jacques, no cleaning.
- I shall resist.

503
00:29:56.795 --> 00:29:59.505
Everybody else, be
as gross as possible.

504
00:29:59.590 --> 00:30:01.048
Think dirty thoughts.

505
00:30:01.133 --> 00:30:04.719
We're going to make this tank so filthy,
the dentist'll have to clean it.

506
00:30:04.803 --> 00:30:06.178
- Good work.

507
00:30:14.479 --> 00:30:17.023
All right, we're here, dudes.

508
00:30:17.107 --> 00:30:19.901
Get ready! Your exit's
coming up, man.

509
00:30:19.985 --> 00:30:23.571
- Where? I don't see it. - Right
there. I see it. I see it.

510
00:30:24.615 --> 00:30:28.409
- You mean the swirling vortex of terror?
- That's it, dude.

511
00:30:28.493 --> 00:30:32.371
- Of course it is.
- First, find your exit buddy.

512
00:30:33.498 --> 00:30:36.626
- Do you have your exit buddy?
- Yes.

513
00:30:36.710 --> 00:30:42.173
Squirt here will now give you a
rundown on proper exiting technique.

514
00:30:42.257 --> 00:30:45.343
Good afternoon. We're going
to have a great jump today.

515
00:30:46.386 --> 00:30:49.555
Crank a hard cutback
as you hit the wall.

516
00:30:49.640 --> 00:30:52.558
There's a screaming bottom
turn, so watch out.

517
00:30:52.643 --> 00:30:55.394
Remember, rip it,
roll it and punch it!

518
00:30:56.605 --> 00:30:59.065
It's like he's trying to
speak to me, I know it.

519
00:30:59.149 --> 00:31:03.861
You're really cute, but I don't know what
you're saying. Say the first thing again.

520
00:31:03.946 --> 00:31:06.906
Okay, Jellyman. Go, go, go!

521
00:31:14.623 --> 00:31:16.499
- Whoa!
- Whoa!

522
00:31:19.252 --> 00:31:20.628
Whoo!

523
00:31:20.921 --> 00:31:22.838
That was fun.

524
00:31:23.382 --> 00:31:25.132
I actually enjoyed that.

525
00:31:25.217 --> 00:31:26.676
Hey, look! Turtles.

526
00:31:28.136 --> 00:31:29.595
Most excellent.

527
00:31:29.680 --> 00:31:35.226
Now, turn your fishy tails round and
swim straight on through to Sydney.

528
00:31:35.310 --> 00:31:36.894
No worries, man.

529
00:31:36.979 --> 00:31:39.522
No worries. Thank
you, Dude Crush.

530
00:31:39.606 --> 00:31:41.816
- Bye.
- See you, Jellyman.

531
00:31:41.900 --> 00:31:44.235
Tell your little dude
I said hi, okay?

532
00:31:44.319 --> 00:31:46.862
- See ya later, dudes.
- Bye, everyone.

533
00:31:47.406 --> 00:31:49.532
Nemo would have loved this.

534
00:31:50.367 --> 00:31:54.245
Hey, Crush. I forgot.
How old are you?

535
00:31:54.329 --> 00:31:56.330
150, dude!

536
00:31:56.415 --> 00:31:59.125
And still young. Rock on!

537
00:31:59.209 --> 00:32:02.503
150. I got to remember that.

538
00:32:03.422 --> 00:32:04.880
Whoa.

539
00:32:09.219 --> 00:32:11.762
- We going in there?
- Yep.

540
00:32:11.847 --> 00:32:13.723
P. Sherman, 42
Wallaby Way, Sydney?

541
00:32:13.807 --> 00:32:14.849
Yep.

542
00:32:15.726 --> 00:32:18.394
We're going to just
swim straight.

543
00:32:19.688 --> 00:32:21.772
Just keep swimming

544
00:32:21.857 --> 00:32:23.274
Dory...

545
00:32:32.576 --> 00:32:35.119
Boy, this
is taking a while.

546
00:32:35.203 --> 00:32:36.662
Hey, how about
we play a game?

547
00:32:36.747 --> 00:32:37.747
Okay.

548
00:32:37.831 --> 00:32:41.167
Okay, I'm thinking
of something orange.

549
00:32:41.251 --> 00:32:43.044
- And it's small...
- It's me.

550
00:32:43.128 --> 00:32:44.170
Right.

551
00:32:44.254 --> 00:32:48.632
This one you'll never guess.
It's orange and small.

552
00:32:48.717 --> 00:32:49.717
It's me.

553
00:32:49.801 --> 00:32:51.677
All righty, Mr. Smarty Pants.

554
00:32:51.762 --> 00:32:55.014
It's orange and small
and white stripes...

555
00:32:55.098 --> 00:32:57.224
Me. And the next one,
just a guess, me.

556
00:32:57.309 --> 00:32:58.517
Okay. That's just scary.

557
00:32:58.602 --> 00:33:01.687
Wait. I've seen this
floating speck before.

558
00:33:01.772 --> 00:33:04.356
That means we've passed it.

559
00:33:04.441 --> 00:33:06.734
That means we're not
going straight.

560
00:33:06.818 --> 00:33:09.779
We got to get to the surface.
We'll figure it out there.

561
00:33:09.863 --> 00:33:11.030
- Hey!
- What?

562
00:33:11.114 --> 00:33:13.407
Relax. Take a deep breath.

563
00:33:17.037 --> 00:33:19.538
Now, let's ask somebody
for directions.

564
00:33:19.623 --> 00:33:22.083
Fine. Who? The speck?
There's nobody here!

565
00:33:22.167 --> 00:33:24.627
There has to be someone.
It's the ocean.

566
00:33:24.711 --> 00:33:27.379
We're not the only two in here.
Let's see...

567
00:33:27.464 --> 00:33:29.256
Okay, no one there.

568
00:33:29.341 --> 00:33:30.841
Nope.

569
00:33:30.926 --> 00:33:32.343
Nada.

570
00:33:34.513 --> 00:33:37.348
- There's somebody.
- Hey, excu... - Dory!

571
00:33:37.432 --> 00:33:39.892
I'm thinking of
something mysterious.

572
00:33:39.976 --> 00:33:44.146
It's a fish we don't know, and if we
ask it directions, it could ingest us.

573
00:33:44.231 --> 00:33:46.732
What is it with men and
asking for directions?

574
00:33:46.817 --> 00:33:50.402
Don't play the gender card. Let's
play the "let's not die" card.

575
00:33:50.487 --> 00:33:52.446
- Want to get out of here?
- Of course.

576
00:33:52.531 --> 00:33:56.575
How are we going to do that unless we
give it a shot and hope for the best?

577
00:33:56.660 --> 00:33:59.745
- You don't fully understand.
- Trust me on this.

578
00:34:08.964 --> 00:34:10.172
All right.

579
00:34:12.384 --> 00:34:14.969
Excuse me? Little fella?

580
00:34:16.346 --> 00:34:17.388
Hello.

581
00:34:17.472 --> 00:34:19.306
Don't be rude. Say hi.

582
00:34:19.391 --> 00:34:21.016
Hello.

583
00:34:21.101 --> 00:34:23.435
- His son Bingo...
- Nemo.

584
00:34:23.520 --> 00:34:25.771
- ...was taken to...
- Sydney.

585
00:34:25.856 --> 00:34:27.189
Sydney, yes.

586
00:34:27.274 --> 00:34:31.068
It's really important that we
get there as fast as we can.

587
00:34:31.153 --> 00:34:32.903
Can you help us out?

588
00:34:33.530 --> 00:34:36.532
Come on, little fella. Come on.

589
00:34:37.951 --> 00:34:39.785
Dory, I'm a little fella.

590
00:34:40.370 --> 00:34:43.164
I don't think that's
a little fella.

591
00:34:45.667 --> 00:34:48.002
Big fella. Whale. Okay.

592
00:34:48.086 --> 00:34:50.212
Maybe he only speaks whale.

593
00:34:51.590 --> 00:34:54.133
We need

594
00:34:54.217 --> 00:34:57.428
to find his son.

595
00:34:57.512 --> 00:35:00.306
What are you doing? Are
you sure you speak whale?

596
00:35:00.390 --> 00:35:03.350
Can you give us...

597
00:35:03.435 --> 00:35:06.478
- Heaven knows what you're saying.
- ... Directions?

598
00:35:06.563 --> 00:35:09.899
- See, he's swimming away.
- Come back.

599
00:35:09.983 --> 00:35:11.609
You've offended him.

600
00:35:11.693 --> 00:35:15.946
Maybe a different dialect.

601
00:35:16.573 --> 00:35:19.742
This is not whale. You're
speaking, like, upset stomach.

602
00:35:19.826 --> 00:35:22.536
- Maybe I should try humpback.
- No, don't.

603
00:35:24.164 --> 00:35:26.749
- You sound sick.
- Maybe louder, huh?

604
00:35:26.833 --> 00:35:28.751
- Don't do that.
- Too much orca.

605
00:35:28.835 --> 00:35:33.672
- Didn't that sound a little orca-ish?
- It sounds like nothing I've ever heard.

606
00:35:36.051 --> 00:35:37.760
Just as well. He
might be hungry.

607
00:35:37.844 --> 00:35:40.846
Whales don't eat clownfish.
They eat krill.

608
00:35:40.931 --> 00:35:43.557
- Swim away!
- Look. Krill!

609
00:35:46.478 --> 00:35:49.104
Move, Dory! Move!

610
00:35:55.278 --> 00:35:58.322
Look at that. Would
you look at that?

611
00:35:58.406 --> 00:36:01.700
Filthy. Absolutely filthy.

612
00:36:01.785 --> 00:36:05.204
And it's all thanks to you, kid.
You made it possible.

613
00:36:05.288 --> 00:36:07.206
Jacques, I said no cleaning.

614
00:36:07.290 --> 00:36:08.374
I am ashamed.

615
00:36:09.000 --> 00:36:10.918
Look. Scum Angel.

616
00:36:15.966 --> 00:36:18.634
Bubbles! I love the bubbles.

617
00:36:19.261 --> 00:36:23.264
Flo? Has anybody seen Flo? Flo!

618
00:36:23.348 --> 00:36:25.474
9:00, and cue dentist.

619
00:36:26.434 --> 00:36:28.143
Barbara. Sorry I'm late.

620
00:36:28.228 --> 00:36:30.437
Okay. Here we go.

621
00:36:30.522 --> 00:36:32.189
Little Davey Reynolds.

622
00:36:32.274 --> 00:36:36.527
- Walks to the counter, drops the keys...
- Bloat, that's disgusting.

623
00:36:36.987 --> 00:36:38.946
Tastes pretty good to me.

624
00:36:40.198 --> 00:36:42.825
Don't you realise we are
swimming in our own...

625
00:36:43.326 --> 00:36:45.411
- Shh! Here he comes.
- What the...

626
00:36:46.997 --> 00:36:48.789
Crikey. What a state.

627
00:36:52.752 --> 00:36:55.921
Barbara, what's my earliest
appointment tomorrow?

628
00:36:56.006 --> 00:36:57.881
- 10:00, love.
- Leave it open.

629
00:36:57.966 --> 00:37:01.468
I've got to clean the fish
tank before Darla gets here.

630
00:37:01.553 --> 00:37:06.432
- You hear that, Sharkbait? - Yay!
- He's going to clean the tank!

631
00:37:06.516 --> 00:37:08.392
Yeah, we're going to be clean!

632
00:37:08.476 --> 00:37:10.394
- Ready to see your dad?
- Uh-huh.

633
00:37:10.478 --> 00:37:11.603
Course you are.

634
00:37:12.063 --> 00:37:17.526
I wouldn't be surprised if he's out there
in the harbour waiting for you right now.

635
00:37:18.320 --> 00:37:19.695
Yeah.
